<Text>&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Phased Array Analysis, 1-stage Receiver&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;This workspace a variety of experiments that show the effect of&amp;nbsp;individual phased-array/beamforming features, compared to the baseline result&amp;nbsp;in Folder 01.&amp;nbsp; In each case you will observe the integrity of the final beam shape, usually expressed as a directivity.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;In most cases you will be either running the PhasedArray analysis controller directly, or right-clicking on the &quot;PlotPattern&quot; script in that folder, and running the MATLAB Script (&quot;Run Equations&quot;), which runs both the analysis, then executes some automated post-processing.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;Description of experiments in each folder: &lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;01 BaseLine_Taylor_Theta30Phi270_Pin-20&lt;/U&gt; :&amp;nbsp; contains the RF beamforming Rx design with 8x8 URA, Taylor window, -20 dBm isotropically received power, and the phase shifters pointing the beam to theta = 30 degree and phi = 270 degree. You can run &quot;PlotPattern&quot; to run the phased array analysis and plot the directivity pattern. You can also&amp;nbsp;access the phased array measurement variables in&amp;nbsp;the dataset.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;02 Compression_Pin0&lt;/U&gt;: Increase the isotropically received power to 0 dBm and observe the amplifier compression effect to the Taylor side lobes.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;03 Saturation_Pin20&lt;/U&gt;: Increase the isotropically received power to&amp;nbsp;20 dBm and observe the amplifier&amp;nbsp;saturation to the Taylor side lobes.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;04 AMPM_Pin0&lt;/U&gt;: Observe the impact of amplifier AM to PM to the directivity pattern with 0 dBm isotropically received power.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;05 PhaseErrorUniform&lt;/U&gt;: Apply phase shift errors with uniform distribution and observe the impact to the directivity pattern.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;06 PhaseErrorNormal&lt;/U&gt;: Apply phase shift errors with&amp;nbsp;normal distribution and observe the impact to the directivity pattern.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;07 AttenuationErrorUniform&lt;/U&gt;: Apply attenuator errors with&amp;nbsp;uniform distribution and observe the impact to the directivity pattern.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;08 AttenuationErrorNormal&lt;/U&gt;: Apply attenuator errors with&amp;nbsp;normal distribution and observe the impact to the directivity pattern.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;09 PhaseQuantization_Theta33Phi255_3bits&lt;/U&gt;: Apply 3-bit phase shifter quantization to the phase shifters pointing the beam to theta = 33 degree and phi = 255 degree.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;10 GainQuantization_3bits&lt;/U&gt;: Apply 3-bit attenuator quantization.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;13 CosineAntenna&lt;/U&gt;: Use CosineAntenna element pattern instead of Isotropic in the antenna array.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;14 CosineAntenna_ElementRotation&lt;/U&gt;: Use CosineAntenna element pattern and rotate each element 45 degree around Y axis.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;U&gt;15 HFSS&lt;/U&gt;: Use HFSS pattern file for each element. Note that the maximum directivity of the HFSS element pattern does not point to theta = 0.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;TIP: for a 3D pattern plot, you can measure the beamwidth and direction using&amp;nbsp;a marker function.&amp;nbsp; Select the 3D trace itself, right-click and add &quot;Marker/Maximum&quot; to&amp;nbsp;put a marker&amp;nbsp;on the tip of the pattern (usually called &quot;m1&quot;).&amp;nbsp; Now select the new marker, and right-click again.&amp;nbsp; Choose &quot;Beamwidth/50% of Max&quot;.&amp;nbsp; You will see the marker measurements in the lower left corner of your 3D plot.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;NOTE: The lineup in the&amp;nbsp;schematics are for demonstration purpose. They are not meant&amp;nbsp;to be a starting point&amp;nbsp;for&amp;nbsp;realistic&amp;nbsp;phased array design.&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
